# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Caribooks Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) using npm with `--legacy-peer-deps` flag
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
**Modified:** `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component in the root layout's body section, right after `<SpeedInsights />`

## Implementation Details

### Framework
This is a **Next.js 15** project using the **App Router** architecture, so I followed the official Vercel documentation's instructions for Next.js App Router.

### Analytics Component Placement
The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) which ensures analytics tracking is active across all pages of the application. It's positioned at the end of the body section, consistent with the existing SpeedInsights component.

### Code Changes
```typescript
// Added import
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'

// Added component in body
<SpeedInsights />
<Analytics />
```

## Verification

### ✅ Type Checking
Ran `npm run typecheck` - No TypeScript errors

### ✅ Build
Ran `npm run build` - Build completed successfully
- All 21 routes compiled and generated correctly
- No errors or warnings related to Analytics

### ✅ Tests
Ran `npm run test` - All tests passed
- 2 test files, 16 tests passed
- No breaking changes introduced

## Next Steps (Deployment)

To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Navigate to the Analytics section in your Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate analytics for the project
4. Verify analytics are working by checking the browser Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Notes
- The Analytics component is placed alongside the existing SpeedInsights component for consistency
- Used `--legacy-peer-deps` flag during installation to resolve peer dependency conflicts with existing Vite/Vitest setup
- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation retrieved from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Analytics will automatically track page views and Web Vitals metrics once enabled in the Vercel dashboard
